### composition with `brod4910/stack/69`

`KVConnector` protocol and `LMCacheConnector` are defined in stack/69. see [appendix: stack/69 details](#stack69-lmcache-details) for full protocol definition, `BlockManager` integration sequence, Mojo kernel architecture, and data path analysis.

`ExternalKVConnector` (this RFC) and `LMCacheConnector` (stack/69) both implement `KVConnector`. migration: stack/69 lands as in-process MVP, then `LMCacheConnector` + `MAXGPUConnector` + Mojo kernels move to manager process. engine gets `ExternalKVConnector` via `create_connector()` when `--kv-manager-endpoint` is set. `BlockManager` calls unchanged.[^18]

|                               | stack/69 (in-process)                             | this RFC (external process)                                                 |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| where `LMCacheConnector` runs | engine process                                    | KV cache manager process                                                    |
| LMCache/torch import          | engine process                                    | manager process only                                                        |
| GPU transfer                  | `MAXGPUConnector` + Mojo kernels (in-process)     | `TransferExecutor` + `Buffer.inplace_copy_from()` to shm                    |
| staging memory                | LMCache `MemoryObj` tensors (in-process)          | POSIX shm with `BlockMeta` atomics                                          |
| save path                     | gather kernel $\to$ LMCache engine (synchronous)  | D2H $\to$ shm (async) $\to$ STORE_NOTIFY $\to$ manager calls LMCache engine |
| load path                     | LMCache engine $\to$ scatter kernel (synchronous) | manager writes shm $\to$ engine H2D from shm (async, pipelined)             |
| crash isolation               | connector dies with engine                        | connector survives engine crash                                             |

Mojo gather/scatter kernels stay in manager process for LMCache `StorageManager` ops. engine side uses `Buffer.inplace_copy_from()` to/from shm, no layout transformation bc shm uses MAX's native paged layout.

